{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Behold, the meaning is that it is not fitting for a person to rely on a person, and if a person is stronger than him, let him rely on Him in his prayer to HaShem. And so if he is hungry or was imprisoned, and so if a disease of the eyes came upon him, or if he was bent, fixed to a bed, let him not rely on a physician." "And the meaning of <b>YHWH loves the righteous</b> — that He guards them, and they shall not be oppressed, nor hungry or imprisoned or blind or bent."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 146, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:56.813251691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}